{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219700-a-few-doubts-about-rules-of-magick","id":1219700,"title":"A few doubts about rules of magick","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-17T10:32:16-07:00","id":1219700,"title":"A few doubts about rules of magick","content":"Hi, I am new to this manual and forums and I would like to ask some cuestions about magick (I hope there are no repeated. I searched in the forums but didn't find out anything).<br /> <br /> 1. I know that wich Correspondence sphere you can uso magick at greater distance but, what is the discance default for magick? (touch, a few meters...).<br /> 2. With Forces 2 you can &quot;push&quot; things that come to you (altering his vector to move in anothe direction). What do I need to this happen in an object lige a shirt or a rock?<br /> 3. How works visual effects trinkets?. If I understand well, a trinket youl be a objet in wich someone used Magick to give it specific properties such as extra resistance, fireproof, extra light, etc, however that some glasses let you use the Correspondence 1 of see the exact distance/measures is listed as a trinket in M20. There is something I misunderstood?.<br /> <br /> PD: Excuse my bad english, I am not a navite speake and reading is by far easier to writing for me. Thanks in advance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24126-bartimeo","name":"Bartimeo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24126_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T12:42:54-07:00","id":1219748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. I know that wich Correspondence sphere you can uso magick at greater distance but, what is the discance default for magick? (touch, a few meters...). </div> </div> </div>The defeault are the Mage's senses - normally in most cases &quot;line of sight&quot; as we are used to using our eyes, but a blind mage might as well use their hearing or sense of smell.<br /> Theoretically it might even be possible to use a sound as a carrier for an effect, but an ST would have to rule if that was possible without Correspondence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. With Forces 2 you can &quot;push&quot; things that come to you (altering his vector to move in anothe direction). What do I need to this happen in an object lige a shirt or a rock? </div> </div> </div>Forces is enough for that. Forces 2 can move up to a human, or around 300 pounds/150 kg. Forces 3 can move two tons. Forces 4 can move 'small buildings'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. How works visual effects trinkets?. If I understand well, a trinket youl be a objet in wich someone used Magick to give it specific properties such as extra resistance, fireproof, extra light, etc, however that some glasses let you use the Correspondence 1 of see the exact distance/measures is listed as a trinket in M20. There is something I misunderstood? </div> </div> </div>Correspondence 1 might be enough for that, as long as the glasses touch you. Sphere 1 senses can be shared by touch, and the TruShades in the M20 book also use those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T14:18:29-07:00","id":1219786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bartimeo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219700-a-few-doubts-about-rules-of-magick#post1219700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. How works visual effects trinkets?. If I understand well, a trinket youl be a objet in wich someone used Magick to give it specific properties such as extra resistance, fireproof, extra light, etc, however that some glasses let you use the Correspondence 1 of see the exact distance/measures is listed as a trinket in M20. There is something I misunderstood?.<br /> <br /> PD: Excuse my bad english, I am not a navite speake and reading is by far easier to writing for me. Thanks in advance</div> </div> </div> </div>Your English is much better than my [whatever your Native Language is] I'm sure. You're doing great.<br /> <br /> As for Trinkets, it should be noted that TruShades are NOT a Trinket. M20 lists them as one. M20 does get a few things wrong, sadly. A trinket has a neat mechanical upshot. A javelin which flies extra far when you throw it, or a window which can't be broken, or a set of brass knuckles which do Aggravated damage. You get the idea. Glasses which let you see REALLY clearly (perhaps -2 difficulty to visual Perception rolls) would be a Trinket. Glasses which apply a Correspondence 1 effect, perfectly measuring the distances between objects... that's not really a Trinket.<br /> <br /> TruShades should be listed as an Artifact/Invention (if they need to be used by a Mage) or a Talisman/Device (if they can also be used by Sleepers). In this case it's much more likely to be a Device. That way the Technocracy can mass produce them for their sleeper operatives (unawakened constructs, extraordinary citizens, mooks).<br /> <br /> As an example...<br /> <br /> A special lighter which helps you start a normal-sized fire really easily is a Trinket.<br /> A lighter which lets a Sleeper generate a huge inferno is a Talisman/Device.<br /> A lighter which can start a huge inferno when used by a Mage is an Artifact/Invention.<br /> <br /> A ring that lets the wearer inflict Aggravated damage (passively) with punches is a Trinket. Here you're rolling your Strength (with any other bonuses) for Aggravated damage.<br /> A ring that lets a Sleeper activate a Forces 2 / Life 3 enhanced punch which inflicts Aggravated damage is a Talisman. Here you roll the Ring's Arete for points of Aggravated damage.<br /> A ring that lets a Mage do that is an Artifact. Here you roll the Mage's Arete for points of Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> And out of those three examples, a Trinket could be best, or a Talisman, or an Artifact. It depends on the situation.<br /> <br /> The important distinction is that in the first case, a normal object is better than normal. It burns hotter, it sparks more easily, the fluid lasts longer... some Matter and Forces with Prime could sort that out. In the second and third case the object isn't just doing something well, it's doing something magickal and wondrous, you might say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-17-2018, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T14:58:45-07:00","id":1219800,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies, I am from Spain if you want to know xD.<br /> <br /> About the second question I don't think I explained myself very well. My question is what is neccesary to have the effect (repulse object coming at you) applied to the object (shirt or rock). If anyone has read the Allow of Law from Brandom Sanderson I am looking for an effect that pushes/redirect projectiles incoming after a certain speed like the protagonist does in order to make himself a hader target and to know how hard would be that the &quot;center&quot; of that effect is an object instead of the mage himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24126-bartimeo","name":"Bartimeo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24126_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T19:16:11-07:00","id":1219858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219700-a-few-doubts-about-rules-of-magick?p=1219786#post1219786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Trinkets, it should be noted that TruShades are NOT a Trinket. M20 lists them as one. M20 does get a few things wrong, sadly. A trinket has a neat mechanical upshot. A javelin which flies extra far when you throw it, or a window which can't be broken, or a set of brass knuckles which do Aggravated damage. You get the idea. Glasses which let you see REALLY clearly (perhaps -2 difficulty to visual Perception rolls) would be a Trinket. Glasses which apply a Correspondence 1 effect, perfectly measuring the distances between objects... that's not really a Trinket.<br /> <br /> TruShades should be listed as an Artifact/Invention (if they need to be used by a Mage) or a Talisman/Device (if they can also be used by Sleepers). In this case it's much more likely to be a Device. That way the Technocracy can mass produce them for their sleeper operatives (unawakened constructs, extraordinary citizens, mooks).</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly wouldn't have as much a problem with the TruShades, if they were described as having a permanent Effect that altered how light passed through the lenses. Making it so the light that comes out is shaped by other layers of reality, like the flows of magic (Prime), the colors of auras (Mind or Spirit), or the whirls and vortices of Time (duh). If it was just that, I might have been okay with it.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the TruShades can be <i>turned off</i>. A mechanism is built into the TruShades, allowing the wearer to turn them on and off at will. Implying a level of sophistication beyond merely an object stuck with a permanent regular Effect, and into the realms of Artifacts or Talismans. As they stand, the TruShades obviously aren't just magic left to dumbly continue its assigned function until the end of time. It's something you use to actively cast prescribed Effects.<br /> <br /> That muddies the waters as to how different kinds of Wonders work. Unhelpful, when you're trying to get a new player interested in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T21:14:05-07:00","id":1219876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bartimeo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219700-a-few-doubts-about-rules-of-magick?p=1219800#post1219800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the replies, I am from Spain if you want to know xD.<br /> <br /> About the second question I don't think I explained myself very well. My question is what is neccesary to have the effect (repulse object coming at you) applied to the object (shirt or rock). If anyone has read the Allow of Law from Brandom Sanderson I am looking for an effect that pushes/redirect projectiles incoming after a certain speed like the protagonist does in order to make himself a hader target and to know how hard would be that the &amp;quot;center&amp;quot; of that effect is an object instead of the mage himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to enchant your shirt to have a repulsive<br /> effect you need Forces 2 (to alter the trajectory of bullets or other stuff flying at you) and Matter 2 (to \u201clock\u201c this effect into the pattern of the shirt).<br /> <br /> In your presence and with concentration you can forego the Matter requirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T02:41:44-07:00","id":1219905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219700-a-few-doubts-about-rules-of-magick?p=1219858#post1219858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly wouldn't have as much a problem with the TruShades, if they were described as having a permanent Effect that altered how light passed through the lenses. Making it so the light that comes out is shaped by other layers of reality, like the flows of magic (Prime), the colors of auras (Mind or Spirit), or the whirls and vortices of Time (duh). If it was just that, I might have been okay with it.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the TruShades can be <i>turned off</i>. A mechanism is built into the TruShades, allowing the wearer to turn them on and off at will. Implying a level of sophistication beyond merely an object stuck with a permanent regular Effect, and into the realms of Artifacts or Talismans. As they stand, the TruShades obviously aren't just magic left to dumbly continue its assigned function until the end of time. It's something you use to actively cast prescribed Effects.<br /> <br /> That muddies the waters as to how different kinds of Wonders work. Unhelpful, when you're trying to get a new player interested in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and furthermore the effect it suggests feels complex enough that you almost wonder what dice you're using for it. If your TruShades highlight distances between things, what do you roll to notice a small spatial anomaly created through use of Correspondence? I mean you could simply roll Perception, but honestly it feels like the glasses need Arete at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T01:26:53-07:00","id":1221415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219700-a-few-doubts-about-rules-of-magick?p=1219876#post1219876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to enchant your shirt to have a repulsive<br /> effect you need Forces 2 (to alter the trajectory of bullets or other stuff flying at you) and Matter 2 (to \u201clock\u201c this effect into the pattern of the shirt).<br /> <br /> In your presence and with concentration you can forego the Matter requirement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Matter 2 needed because the os a effect of Forces 2, because is a &quot;simple&quot; material like a short or is it always Sphere iof patron 2 to &quot;lock&quot; an effect no matter wich one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24126-bartimeo","name":"Bartimeo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24126_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T06:01:14-07:00","id":1221673,"title":"","content":"Locking an effect requires a Patern Sphere at the rank required to make a change to the patern in question.<br /> <br /> To lock ANY effect to an object you need Mater 2 for a simple object (rock, shirt, hammer). For a complex object (car, gun, computer) you would need Mater 4.<br /> <br /> For living creatures you would need Life 3 for yourself or Life 4 for others.<br /> <br /> You only need to Lock effects if you want them to stay active away from you presence or if you don't want to maintain concentration on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T09:43:17-07:00","id":1221737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219700-a-few-doubts-about-rules-of-magick?p=1221673#post1221673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Locking an effect requires a Patern Sphere at the rank required to make a change to the patern in question.<br /> <br /> To lock ANY effect to an object you need Mater 2 for a simple object (rock, shirt, hammer). For a complex object (car, gun, computer) you would need Mater 4.<br /> <br /> For living creatures you would need Life 3 for yourself or Life 4 for others.<br /> <br /> You only need to Lock effects if you want them to stay active away from you presence or if you don't want to maintain concentration on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming that to lock an effect onto someone's shadow, you'd need Forces 2? So if you wanted to make a person's shadow loom over them threateningly whenever they considered betraying you (complex Forces + Mind stuff there) then you could &quot;lock&quot; the effect onto a Forces Pattern. After all, Spirit and Forces are Pattern Spheres too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T10:19:26-07:00","id":1221749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219700-a-few-doubts-about-rules-of-magick?p=1221737#post1221737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm assuming that to lock an effect onto someone's shadow, you'd need Forces 2? So if you wanted to make a person's shadow loom over them threateningly whenever they considered betraying you (complex Forces + Mind stuff there) then you could &quot;lock&quot; the effect onto a Forces Pattern. After all, Spirit and Forces are Pattern Spheres too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice idea! . Very thematic for some Paradigms.<br /> <br /> I think it should require Forces 3, because 3 it's the level that allows to transmute force patterns (Interestingly, Forces and Matter are inverse at this. Matter changes shapes at 3 and substance at 2, Forces changes shape at 2 and substance at 3).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T10:36:56-07:00","id":1221757,"title":"","content":"Shadow would be Forces 3 though likely fleeting as it would fail everytime it disappeared. Remember there are no shadows in the dark.<br /> <br /> Spirit was Spirit 3 for self and 4 for others in revised. For some reason I thought M20 made it all Spirit 4. I'd have to look that one up again. The Taftini had a rote that enchanted forcefields to their spirit in Lost Paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 05-24-2018, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T11:27:40-07:00","id":1221774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1219700-a-few-doubts-about-rules-of-magick?p=1221757#post1221757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow would be Forces 3 though likely fleeting as it would fail everytime it disappeared. Remember there are no shadows in the dark.<br /> <br /> Spirit was Spirit 3 for self and 4 for others in revised. For some reason I thought M20 made it all Spirit 4. I'd have to look that one up again. The Taftini had a rote that enchanted forcefields to their spirit in Lost Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends however. If your paradigm thinks of darkness as its own entity, rather than the absence of light (much as many shamans think of &quot;cold&quot; as its own force), then there's no reason for such a spell to simply fade when there shadow isn't currently *visible*. If you were to curse a person's voice, so that all who hear them speak do not believe them, that curse would not be active while they're not speaking, of course. But it's the same with the shadow. If they were in a room with absolute lighting then the shadow wouldn't be able to influence them, but most of the time it would.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, cursing someone's voice so people won't listen to them... Entropy and Forces and Mind or Entropy and Life and Mind? I feel like either would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}